:name: Launchpad Pro MK3 — interactive
:description: Runs a firmware ELF with the M0 model's front-panel socket on TCP 3456; start renode with -P 1234 for the monitor port.
# usage: renode --disable-gui -P 1234 -e '$elf=@/path/fw.elf; include @run.resc'
#        then: python3 ../m0/panel_bridge.py and open http://localhost:8765

$elf?=@../corefw/target/thumbv7em-none-eabihf/release/core
# instructions per virtual second, in millions (216 = 216 MHz at 1 IPC).
# Boot runs at $bootmips (boot only busy-waits on timeouts); the M0 model raises it to $runmips
# once its button stream is up.
$bootmips?=50
$runmips?=216

include @STM32_TimerLP.cs
include @STM32DMA_LP.cs
include @LPPM0.cs
include @LPPOTGFS.cs
include @LPPDIN.cs
include @LPPSpiFlash.cs
using sysbus
mach create "lppmk3"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @lppmk3.repl

sysbus LoadELF $elf
cpu PerformanceInMips $bootmips
cpu VectorTableOffset 0x08010000
cpu SP `sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x08010000`
cpu PC `sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x08010004`

m0 StreamUpMips $runmips
m0 StartPanel 3456
usbOtgFs StartBridge 3457
din StartBridge 3458
$flash?=$ORIGIN/flash.bin
spi1.spiFlash UseFile $flash

logLevel 3
logLevel 2 uart5
logLevel 1 usbOtgFs
start
